  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;\">The University of Nottingham Malaysia (UNM) is the first ever branch campus of a British university established outside the UK. Founded in 2000, you will find yourself at a premier institution that offers the same world-class curriculum and degrees as the University of Nottingham in the UK. The university is a member of the prestigious Russell Group and sits on a stunning 48-hectare (125-acre) site in Semenyih, which is designed to mirror the attributes of University Park in Nottingham. You can choose from a wide array of Foundation, Undergraduate, and Postgraduate programmes across two main faculties: the Faculty of Arts and Social Sciences and the Faculty of Science and Engineering.</span></p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;\">You will be part of a vibrant, global community with over 5,000 students from more than 85 different countries. Life on campus is designed to be inclusive and engaging, featuring a dedicated Students’ Association Building (Blocks H and H1) where you can access meeting rooms, music rooms, a dance studio, and even games rooms with pool and foosball tables. If you enjoy the outdoors, the campus features a scenic jogging track around the main lake and an amphitheatre for concerts and recitals.</span></p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>UNM offers extensive on-campus housing through 11 halls of residence, providing approximately 2,400 beds. You can choose from various room configurations to suit your budget:</p><ul><li><strong>Student Village North (J Halls):</strong> Features newer accommodations with options like Super Deluxe Single Ensuite rooms.</li><li><strong>Student Village South (I Halls):</strong> Offers classic campus living with shared pantry lounges. Rooms range from four-shared rooms to single ensuite units with air conditioning. Each floor includes a pantry for light cooking. If you prefer living off-site, there are nearby private options like Taman Tasik Semenyih and UniVillage.</li></ul>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Facilities",
      "value": "<p>&nbsp;<strong>Library</strong> The University of Nottingham Malaysia Library is a central hub for your academic success, providing extensive physical collections, digital databases, and quiet study zones. You will also have access to the same digital resources available to students at the UK and China campuses.</p><p><strong>Sports</strong> You will have access to a purpose-built Sports Complex that includes:</p><ol><li>An outdoor swimming pool.</li><li>Indoor gyms and outdoor gym stations.</li><li>Facilities for football, hockey, rugby, cricket, and basketball.</li><li>Squash and tennis courts, as well as an archery range.</li></ol><p><strong>Laboratories</strong> For science and engineering students, UNM provides state-of-the-art research and teaching labs. Notable facilities include the <strong>High-Performance Computing (HPC)</strong> system deployed in partnership with NVIDIA to advance research in Artificial Intelligence and machine learning.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Cafeteria</strong> Dining on campus is a diverse experience. You can find several F&amp;B outlets in Blocks H and H1, including:</p><ol><li><strong>Bistro 1:</strong> Serving Indian Muslim (Mamak) cuisine.</li><li><strong>18 Grams Coffee &amp; ZUS Coffee:</strong> For your caffeine and pastry fix.</li><li><strong>Zafa Café:</strong> Offering Malay Fusion dishes.</li><li>Specialised stalls for Japanese, Arabic, Thai, Chinese, and Vegan food.</li></ol>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Campuses",
      "value": "<ol><li>&nbsp;</li></ol><h4><strong>Semenyih (Main Campus)</strong></h4><p>Located about 30km south of Kuala Lumpur, the Semenyih campus is a self-contained \"garden village.\" It serves as the primary academic and residential hub. You will find that everything is within walking distance, and the university provides a free shuttle bus service connecting you to local amenities and the Kajang KTM/MRT stations for easy access to the city centre.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
